To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: Re: X with ATI Rage 128
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=103762625703882

Ryan Cooley wrote (in a message from Monday 18)
 > I've got OpenBSD/Alpha 3.2 installed and working just fine on my DEC
 > Personal Workstation 500au.  In order to get my ATI card working, I
 > simply changed the video driver to "ati" (and inserted a 'DefaultDepth
 > 16' line since I don't like 8bpp).  
 > 
 > I tried 'XFree86 -configure', as well as 'xf86config' but neither
 > created a usable config file.  My one question; is 640x480 the max
 > resolution?  Inserting a 'Modes' section has zero effect, and the fact
 > that the section was left out strikes me as a sign that the X server
 > can't do any better.
 > 

The ati driver has not yet been tested on alpha. So many tings can
happen. However, it's hard to tell without seeing the full
/var/log/XFree86.0.log file which may explain what's happening. 

The most probable cause if you're stuck at 640x480 is that the
bandwidth of your monitor is specified incorrectly in the Monitor
section of XF86Config. Another possible cause is an incorrect detecion
of the available video ram. 


					Matthieu

